  {
    "page_content": "Approval must be documented and retained in the order file.\n4. Order Backlog Management\n4.1 Review Frequency\nOrder Backlog is reviewed on a MONTHLY basis by the Finance team.\n4.2 Aging Calculation\nAging (Days) = Current Date - Original Order Booking Date\nAging (Months) = Aging (Days) ÷ 30 (approximate)\n4.3 Flagging Criteria\nBacklog items shall be flagged for review when EITHER:\n- Aging (Days) > 180 days (6 months), OR\n- No delivery milestone has been recorded in the system for 2 consecutive monthly review cycles\nFlagged items require Finance Manager review to determine whether continued recognition remains appropriate.\nCONTROL ENHANCEMENT\nReview frequency moved from quarterly to monthly; aging flag threshold reduced from 365 days to 180 days.\n5. Roles and Responsibilities",
